  "body": "the following code shows 'UTF-8' with Chrome Canary, Safari TP, and Firefox Nightly.\r\n\r\n```\r\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n<form>\r\n<input type=hidden name=\"_charset_\">\r\n</form>\r\n<script>\r\nvar fd = new FormData(document.querySelector('form'));\r\nalert(fd.get('_charset_'));\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\n\r\nhttps://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-formdata\r\n> 2. If form is given, set fd’s entries to the result of constructing the form data set for form.\r\n\r\nThis means the special handling for ```_charset_``` is in \"construct the form data set\" though the current specifications does it in each of form encoding. [application/x-www-form-urlencoded](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-urlencoded-serializerl) [multipart/form-data](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#multipart/form-data-encoding-algorithm) [text/plain](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#text/plain-encoding-algorithm)\r\n\r\nI couldn't test Edge because Edge has no FormData.prototype.get.\r\n",
